# The batch 56 to 58

`Sendov.R_le_batch` bounds every `R n α` for `56 ≤ n ≤ 58` by the elementary part and
moment at `n₀ = 56` together with the prefactor at `n₁ = 58`, so one moment and one
certificate serve all 3 degrees.  The certificate has degree 54, set by `n₀` rather
than `n₁`.

Feasibility at `n₀` is proved rather than assumed: for `n ≥ 36` it follows from
`0 ≤ α ≤ 17`, since `A - c²` increases with `n`.  This matters because feasibility propagates
*upward* in `n`, so it could not be inherited from the hypothesis at `n`.

The moment numerator `Nmomc` is checked against the packed recurrence
(`Sendov.pev_wsum_eq_of_packed`), and the numerator `Sendov.batchP 56 58 26 Lc Nmomc` of
`1 - bound` is certified positive on `[0, 17]` by its Bernstein coefficients `Bc`
(`Sendov.pev_pos_of_bern`).  Every closed computation is evaluated by the kernel.
